/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124055","id":5960263592,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABY0JnqA","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-02T19:52:06Z","updated_at":"2026-10-02T19:52:06Z","body":"Why not change the internal behaviour of `get_script`, while binding a `Variant` based version for compat? The internal API doesn't have to be stable, and it's common to bind alternative implementations that work with the binding types.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5960263592/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5988745890","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124055#issuecomment-5988745890","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124055","id":5988745890,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABZPUCog","user":{"login":"aurpine","id":12262539,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMjYyNTM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12262539?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine","html_url":"https://github.com/aurpine","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-05T05:36:00Z","updated_at":"2026-10-05T05:36:00Z","body":"Not sure if I did it right. The new function is named `get_scriptv` and is the one that is binded to `get_script`. I didn't use the deprecated ifdef because we still use it internally.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5988745890/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5989115508","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124055#issuecomment-5989115508","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124055","id":5989115508,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABZPqmdA","user":{"login":"NoctemCat","id":22471296,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDcxMjk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22471296?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat","html_url":"https://github.com/NoctemCat","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-05T06:13:18Z","updated_at":"2026-10-05T06:17:17Z","body":"I believe if method is just for the bindings, it is named with the same name, but with `_bind` attached, you can search `_bind(` in the `object.cpp` file to see some of them.\r\n\r\nThe `v(` endings seems to be for virtual methods that are designed to be overriden for normal use (except `callv`), I don't think `get_script` fits, but I could be wrong here. Edit: They seem to be used for `GDCLASS`/`GDSOFTCLASS` specifically? \r\n\r\nYou should be able to remove `DEBUG_VIRTUAL` from the bind if you make the bind call the new `get_script`, like:\r\n```C++\r\nVariant Object::_get_script_bind() const {\r\n\tScript *s = get_script();\r\n\treturn s ? Variant(s) : Variant();\r\n}\r\n```\r\n`get_script` then will then call the debug override if it has one.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5989115508/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5989577456","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124055#issuecomment-5989577456","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124055","id":5989577456,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABZQGy8A","user":{"login":"aurpine","id":12262539,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMjYyNTM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12262539?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine","html_url":"https://github.com/aurpine","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-05T06:51:34Z","updated_at":"2026-10-05T06:51:34Z","body":"Thanks I didn't know the conventions. I thought v for variant.\r\n\r\nI implemented it slightly differently:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nScript *s = get_script();\r\nreturn script_instance ? Variant(s) : Variant();\r\n```\r\n\r\nIn the case that script_instance is not null but the script is null, this keeps the same behaviour as before. Not sure if this is possible though...\r\n\r\nAlso I didn't prefix with underscore since it has to be public. Not sure on that convention.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5989577456/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]